From: Z User <z@container>
Date: Mon, 28 Sep 2026 23:05:49 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] =?UTF-8?q?x86:=20complete=20the=20audit=20findings=20?=
 =?UTF-8?q?=E2=80=94=20monitor-family=20matrix,=20string-op=20segment=20sc?=
 =?UTF-8?q?an,=20imul/data16=20laws=20(GAS=202.47-probed)?=
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Review-AI audit response on the operand-direction round, every fix
re-probed against GAS 2.47.20260726 (--64 and --32) and pinned by new
casefile sections; asm-diff sweeps: x86-64 1312/1312, i686 600/600.

P0 fixes (audit-confirmed divergences):
- i686 1-operand `imul` double 0x66 regression: the operand-size push in
  encode_imul now applies to the 2/3-operand forms only; the unary form
  keeps encode_unary_rm's own single prefix (`imul %ax` = 66 f7 e8).
- String-op segment scan: the "ES on the EDI side" and default-drop arms
  `continue` instead of `break`, so a second operand's override survives
  (`cmpsb %es:(%edi),%fs:(%esi)` = 64 a6); a non-string instruction with
  overrides on TWO memory operands is now rejected outright, matching
  GAS (`movl %ds:(%eax),%fs:(%ebx)` errors even with a redundant
  default).
- String-ness is decided by operand SHAPE (no vector register), not by
  the stem: SSE `movsd`/`cmpsd`/`movsq`/`cmpsq` stem-strip to the string
  stems but keep the generic segment law (`movsd %es:(%edi),%xmm0` =
  26 f2 0f 10 07 — ES kept; `movsd %fs:(%edi),%xmm0` accepted).
- i686 `movsl (mem),(mem)` two-memory string arm added (`a5`), mirroring
  movsb/movsw.
- x86-64 monitor-family: one matrix-probed law replaces the hint-only
  check — implicit register NUMBERS are fixed per template
  (monitor/monitorx (0,1,2), mwait (0,1), mwaitx (0,1,3)); monitor/
  monitorx pin slots 1+2 to one width class and free the hint
  (`monitor %rax,%ecx,%edx` = 0f 01 c8 with no 67, `monitor
  %eax,%rcx,%rdx` = 67 0f 01 c8, mixed widths rejected); mwait/mwaitx
  pin all slots to one width class; 16/8-bit spellings are "operand size
  mismatch", EGPRs "operand type mismatch"; only monitor/monitorx carry
  the 0x67 and it follows the hint spelling. This also fixes the x64
  mwaitx code/comment mismatch and extends the i686 trailing-slot law
  (ecx,edx exact — `monitor %eax,%ecx,%ebx` now rejects).

Beyond the audit's list, the same sweep found and fixes:
- i686 monitor/monitorx accepted wrong slot-2 registers (`monitor
  %eax,%ecx,%ebx`): the trailing slots are now ecx,edx exactly.
- i686 `test.s` never flipped the ModR/M roles (`test.s %edx,%ecx` was
  85 d1, GAS says 85 ca) — commutative does not exempt the encoding.

P1/P2 fixes:
- x86-64 `data16` on direct branches now mirrors the i686 law: rel16
  displacement + R_X86_64_PC16 (GAS 2.47 objdump-verified: `data16 jmp
  foo` = 66 e9 0000 + PC16, `data16 je foo` = 66 0f 84 0000, `data16
  call foo` = 66 e8 0000); `data16` + `@PLT` rejects with GAS's "4-byte
  relocation cannot be applied to 2-byte field".
- vmovd/vmovq xmm<->xmm is pinned as casefile contract after 2.47
  probing (`vmovd %xmm4,%xmm6` = 62 f1 7e 08 7e f4, `vmovq %xmm1,%xmm2`
  = c5 fa 7e d1) — resolving the "accept-but-untested" limbo.
- R_386_GOTPC addend finalization only rewrites the sentinel addend 0,
  so a future nonzero addend survives.
- `data16` fixup in 32-bit mode splices before 0x62/0xC4/0xC5/0xD5 —
  they are BOUND/LES/LDS/AAD opcodes there, not prefixes (`data16 bound
  %eax,(%ebx)` = 66 62 03, `data16 aad` = 66 d5 0a).
- Style: the ALU symbol path stops allocating a zero Vec per immediate;
  the i686 registers.rs operand import is hoisted to the top.

Casefiles: new tests/asm-diff/i686/suffix-s.casefile (i686 .s matrix,
unary width pins, string-segment law, SSE movsd segments), x86-64
monitor_family matrix + reject sections, i686 monitor rejects, x86-64
data16 branch + reject sections — every accept line byte-probed on 2.47
before landing. The prior "displacement union bounds" claim is
retracted: the old and new bound expressions were mathematically
identical; the hunk is documentation-only.
